\p \v 15 \w Then|strong="H01961"\w* \w on the seventh|strong="H07637"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w*, \w they got up|strong="H07925"\w* \w at dawn|strong="H05927"\w* \w and marched around|strong="H05437"\w* \w the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w seven|strong="H07651"\w* \w times|strong="H06471"\w* \w in the same|strong="H02088"\w* \w manner|strong="H04941"\w*. \w That|strong="H01931"\w* \w was the only|strong="H07535"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w* \w they circled|strong="H05437"\w* \w the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w seven|strong="H07651"\w* \w times|strong="H06471"\w*. \v 16 \w After the seventh|strong="H07637"\w* \w time around|strong="H06471"\w*, \w the priests|strong="H03548"\w* \w blew|strong="H08628"\w* \w the horns|strong="H07782"\w*, \w and Joshua|strong="H03091"\w* \w commanded|strong="H00559"\w* \w the people|strong="H05971"\w*, “\w Shout|strong="H07321"\w*! \w For|strong="H03588"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w has given|strong="H05414"\w* you \w the city|strong="H05892"\w*! \v 17 \w Now the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w and everything|strong="H03605"\w* in it \w must be|strong="H01961"\w* \w devoted|strong="H02764"\w* \w to the LORD for destruction|strong="H03068"\w*.\f + \fr 6:17 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verses 18 and 21.\f* \w Only|strong="H07535"\w* \w Rahab|strong="H07343"\w* \w the prostitute|strong="H02181"\w* \w and all those|strong="H03605"\w* \w with her|strong="H00854"\w* \w in her house|strong="H01004"\w* \w will live|strong="H02421"\w*, \w because|strong="H03588"\w* \w she hid|strong="H02244"\w* \w the spies|strong="H04397"\w* \w we sent|strong="H07971"\w*. \v 18 \w But|strong="H07535"\w* \w keep away|strong="H08104"\w* \w from|strong="H04480"\w* \w the things devoted to destruction|strong="H02764"\w*, \w lest|strong="H06435"\w* \w you yourself be set apart for destruction|strong="H02763"\w*. \w If you take|str