\p \v 7 \w And these are|strong="H00428"\w* \w the kings|strong="H04428"\w* \w of the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H03091"\w* \w and the Israelites|strong="H01121"\w* \w conquered|strong="H05221"\w* \w beyond|strong="H05676"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H03383"\w* \w to the west|strong="H03220"\w*, \w from Baal-gad|strong="H01171"\w* \w in the Valley|strong="H01237"\w* \w of Lebanon|strong="H03844"\w* \w to|strong="H05704"\w* \w Mount|strong="H02022"\w* \w Halak|strong="H02510"\w*, \w which rises|strong="H05927"\w* \w toward Seir|strong="H08165"\w* (\w according to the allotments|strong="H04256"\w* \w to the tribes|strong="H07626"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w Joshua|strong="H03091"\w* \w gave them|strong="H05414"\w* \w as an inheritance|strong="H03425"\w* \v 8 \w the hill country|strong="H02022"\w*, \w the foothills|strong="H08219"\w*,\f + \fr 12:8 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \w the Arabah|strong="H06160"\w*, \w the slopes|strong="H00794"\w*, \w the wilderness|strong="H04057"\w*, \w and the Negev|strong="H05045"\w* — \w the lands of the Hittites|strong="H02850"\w*, \w Amorites|strong="H00567"\w*, \w Canaanites|strong="H03669"\w*, \w Perizzites|strong="H06522"\w*, \w Hivites|strong="H02340"\w*, \w and Jebusites|strong="H02983"\w*):
